rate closing loopholes (file: /Users/pfleidi/.agents/superpowers-skills/skills/meta/testing-skills-with-subagents/SKILL.md)\n- Tracing Knowledge Lineages: Understand how ideas evolved over time to find old solutions for new problems and avoid repeating past failures (file: /Users/pfleidi/.agents/superpowers-skills/skills/research/tracing-knowledge-lineages/SKILL.md)\n- Using Git Worktrees: Create isolated git worktrees with smart directory selection and safety verification (file: /Users/pfleidi/.agents/superpowers-skills/skills/collaboration/using-git-worktrees/SKILL.md)\n- Verification Before Completion: Run verification commands and confirm output before claiming success (file: /Users/pfleidi/.agents/superpowers-skills/skills/debugging/verification-before-completion/SKILL.md)\n- When Stuck - Problem-Solving Dispatch: Dispatch to the right problem-solving technique based on how you're stuck (file: /Users/pfleidi/.agents/superpowers-skills/skills/problem-solving/when-stuck/SKILL.md)\n- Writing Plans: Create detailed implementation plans with bite-sized tasks for engineers with zero codebase context (file: /Users/pfleidi/.agents/superpowers-skills/skills/collaboration/writing-plans/SKILL.md)\n- Writing Skills: TDD for process documentation - test with subagents before writing, iterate until bulletproof (file: /Users/pfleidi/.agents/superpowers-skills/skills/meta/writing-skills/SKILL.md)\n- pr: Create a pull request for the current branch. Discovers and deduplicates the project's build/lint/test setup from Makefile, mise, CI config, or README and runs verification before pushing. Automatically fixes any verification failures and prompts the user to commit before proceeding. Accepts an optional base branch (defaults to main). Use when the user says \"create pr\", \"open pr\", \"make pr\", or \"/pr\". (file: /Users/pfleidi/.agents/skills/pr/SKILL.md)\n- pr-feedback: Fetch PR review comments, separate human from bot feedback, and address them differently. Human comments are addressed one at a time with user approval. Bot comments are batched and fixed in one pass. No commits are made — code changes only, user commits on their own terms. Accepts an optional PR number or URL; defaults to the PR for the current branch. Use when the user says \"fix pr comments\", \"address pr feedback\", \"pr feedback\", or \"/pr-feedback\". (file: /Users/pfleidi/.agents/skills/pr-feedback/SKILL.md)\n- prompt-master: Generates optimized prompts for any AI tool. Use when writing, fixing, improving, or adapting a prompt for LLM, Cursor, Midjourney, image AI, video AI, coding agents, or any other AI tool. (file: /Users/pfleidi/.agents/skills/prompt-master/SKILL.md)\n- review: Parallel multi-lens code review against the correct base branch. Spawns security, correctness, and simplification agents simultaneously, verifies findings against source, and presents a deduplicated severity-ranked report. User chooses fix mode: supervised, batched, or threshold. No commits are made — code changes only, user commits on their own terms. Use when the user says \"review\", \"review this branch\", \"code review\", \"full review\", or \"/review\". (file: /Users/pfleidi/.agents/skills/review/SKILL.md)\n### How to use skills\n- Discovery: The list above is the skills available in this session (name + description + file path). Skill bodies live on disk at the listed paths.\n- Trigger rules: If the user names a skill (with `$SkillName` or plain text) OR the task clearly matches a skill's description shown above, you must use that skill for that turn. Multiple mentions mean use them all. Do not carry skills across turns unless re-mentioned.\n- Missing/blocked: If a named skill isn't in the list or the path can't be read, say so briefly and continue with the best fallback.\n- How to use a skill (progressive disclosure):\n  1) After deciding to use a skill, open its `SKILL.md`. Read only enough to follow the workflow.\n  2) When `SKILL.md` references relative paths (e.g., `scrip