{"timestamp":"2026-05-05T23:37:57.551Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"I agree with the direction. The current uncommitted `rotateCurrentIfBatchFull()` makes the packer harder to reason about, and I would not commit it as-is.\n\nThe clearer model should be:\n\n- `pending` means: migrated raw transcript checkpoints not yet written to any v2 `/full/*` ref.\n- When `pending` reaches the threshold, archive it directly to a numbered `/full/<n>` generation.\n- When migration ends with a partial batch, write that remainder to `/full/current`.\n- Do not have migration own a second copy of rotation logic.\n\nA scoped plan would be:\n\n1. Replace ambiguous names:\n   - `flush()` -> something like `archivePendingBatch`\n   - `finalize()` -> something like `finishPacking`\n   - `writePendingToCurrent()` -> something like `writeFinalPartialBatchToCurrent`\n\n2. Make `finishPacking` read like the policy:\n   - if there is a final partial batch, write it to `/full/current`\n   - otherwise, if archived batches were written and this was a fresh migration, ensure empty `/full/current`\n\n3. Remove the current uncommitted `rotateCurrentIfBatchFull()` implementation.\n   - That keeps the original regression fix clear: under-threshold migrations never create `/full/0000000000001`.\n   - The boundary case from review finding #3 should be handled separately only by reusing/exporting the existing checkpoint rotation mechanism, not by duplicating it inside `generationPacker`.\n\nSo yes: I’d revise the current uncommitted step before continuing. The immediate cleanup should make the packer encode the migration policy directly, and defer the “existing current + partial reaches threshold” behavior until it can reuse the real rotation path.","phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":null}}
