.\n>\n> **Suggested fix:** Replace the final reset with `CheckAndSetReference(orphanRef, postArchiveRef)` or equivalent. If the CAS fails, leave the concurrent writer’s ref intact and report no completed rotation.\n\n**Improvements (follow-up)**\n\n> **#3** · Low · simplification · `cmd/entire/cli/migrate.go:269`\n>\n> **Issue:** Migration hard-codes archived generation ref formatting with `%013d` instead of reusing the checkpoint package’s generation-ref format.\n>\n> **Impact if not fixed:** Migration and normal rotation can drift if archived generation formatting changes.\n>\n> **Trade-offs:** Adds a small exported helper or moves formatting behind an existing checkpoint package API.\n>\n> **Evidence:** Migration uses `fmt.Sprintf(\"%s%013d\", ...)`; checkpoint rotation owns `generationRefWidth` and uses `%0*d`.\n>\n> **Suggested fix:** Add a checkpoint helper for archived full generation ref names and use it from both migration and rotation.\n\nSummary: 2 required findings, both race conditions around ref updates; 1 low follow-up improvement. The branch is not merge-ready until #1 and #2 are fixed.\n\n**How would you like to proceed?**\n\n1. **Supervised** — I fix one required finding at a time and wait for your approval before the next.\n2. **Batched** — I fix all required findings in the order presented and show a combined diff at the end. You can optionally specify a subset or include improvement findings.\n\nYou can also drop, reorder, or skip any findings.","completed_at":1778028005,"duration_ms":266027,"time_to_first_token_ms":6411}}
