rGeneration = 100`.\n\nSo the regression is: migration treats the rotation threshold as a packing batch size and archives the final partial batch at process finalization, while normal writes only archive after the threshold is reached.\n</root_cause_summary>\n\n<introducing_pr>\nPR that introduced the regression:\n- PR #1091: \"Fix v2 checkpoint migration generation packing\"\n- URL: https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1091\n- Merge commit: `7b871ec72dc899e6ca64e1ef1a4d26613db628f5`\n- Head branch: `fix/entire-migrate-checkpoint-order`\n\nSpecific commits in that PR:\n- `949c27e1d50be14b78b3ceb3bce7428d86151f43` (`Pack migrated checkpoint generations chronologically`) first changed migration to collect raw transcripts and write them into numbered archived `/full/<n>` generations. Its test expected 5 checkpoints with batch size 2 to create three archived refs, including a final 1-checkpoint generation.\n- `8ee3ff03e05d554f3e34f2d670a4aff5babda3d9` (`Address review findings on migration and repair helpers`) refactored that behavior into the current `generationPacker`. The current bug is visible in `generationPacker.finalize`, which flushes pending checkpoints unconditionally.\n</introducing_pr>\n\n<task>\nImplement a minimal fix so `entire migrate --checkpoints v2` does not create a numbered archived `refs/entire/checkpoints/v2/full/<n>` generation when the number of migrated checkpoints is below the rotation threshold.\n\nLikely desired behavior:\n- Full batches at or above `migrateMaxCheckpointsPerGeneration` can still archive into `/full/<n>`.\n- A final partial batch should remain in `/full/current` or otherwise avoid creating a numbered archived generation until the threshold is reached.\n- Preserve existing migration goals: chronological ordering, bounded memory, force-migration pruning, raw transcript readability, task metadata preservation, generation metadata on archived refs, and idempotent reruns.\n\nDo not make broad refactors. Keep the diff scoped to migration packing and directly related tests.\n</task>\n\n<constraints>\n- Follow the repo's AGENTS.md workflow: for this non-trivial behavior change, read source and produce an implementation plan first; wait for approval before editing.\n- Do not commit.\n- Do not add dependencies.\n- Do not rename or reorganize unrelated code.\n- If editing Go files, run: `go build ./...`, `go vet ./...`, and the project lint task (`mise run lint`) before completion.\n- Also run focused migration tests, at minimum: `go test ./cmd/entire/cli -run 'TestMigrateCheckpointsV2|TestPruneV2CheckpointForForce' -count=1`.\n</constraints>\n\n<test_guidance>\nAdd/adjust tests in `cmd/entire/cli/migrate_test.go`.\n\nCoverage needed:\n1. Regression test: set `migrateMaxCheckpointsPerGeneration = 5`, migrate 3 v1 checkpoints, assert:\n   - `v2Store.ListArchivedGenerations()` is empty.\n   - `/full/current` exists and contains 3 checkpoints.\n   - migrated raw transcripts remain readable via `v2Store.ReadSessionContent`.\n2. Existing tests that currently expect final partial archived batches probably need expectation updates:\n   - `TestMigrateCheckpointsV2_PacksFullGenerationsOldestFirst`\n   - `TestMigrateCheckpointsV2_RerunPacksCheckpointsMissingFullArtifacts`\n   - force/repair tests that currently assume fresh migration always leaves `/full/current` empty.\n3. Keep a test for threshold-sized migration archiving so we do not break actual rotation behavior.\n</test_guidance>\n\n<helpful_commands>\nInspect current behavior:\n- `sed -n '180,540p' cmd/entire/cli/migrate.go`\n- `sed -n '698,720p' cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/v2_committed.go`\n- `sed -n '22,30p' cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/v2_generation.go`\n\nHistory:\n- `git show --stat --format=fuller 7b871ec72dc899e6ca64e1ef1a4d26613db628f5`\n- `git show 949c27e1d50be14b78b3ceb3bce7428d86151f43 -- cmd/entire/cli/migrate.go cmd/entire/cli/migrate_test.go`\n- `git show 8ee3ff03e05d554f3e34f2d670a4aff5babda3d9 -- cmd/entire/cli/migrate.go`\n</helpful_com