{"timestamp":"2026-05-06T01:02:43.834Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"Yes, for the normal checkpoint write path.\n\nIf `/full/current` changes between `postArchiveRef` and the reset CAS, `resetFullCurrentRefIfUnchanged` returns `(false, nil)` on `storage.ErrReferenceHasChanged`, logs it, and leaves the newer `/full/current` untouched. Then `RotateCurrentGenerationIfNeeded` returns `archiveRefName, false, nil` from [v2_generation.go](/Users/pfleidi/entire/cli/.worktrees/fix/checkpoints-v2-generation-refs-during-migration/cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/v2_generation.go:560).\n\nFor a normal new checkpoint, the writer calls `rotateCurrentIfNeeded` immediately after updating `/full/current` in [v2_committed.go](/Users/pfleidi/entire/cli/.worktrees/fix/checkpoints-v2-generation-refs-during-migration/cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/v2_committed.go:808). So if that concurrent write pushed the generation over the threshold, it will try rotation on its own updated ref.\n\nThe important behavior is: we do not reset over someone else’s newer current ref. If that newer ref is still at or above threshold, either the concurrent writer’s own post-write rotation handles it, or a later checkpoint write will hit the threshold check again.","phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":null}}
